(a) Process. Any person, association, partnership or corporation desiring to obtain a license to operate, engage in, conduct, or carry on any adult entertainment establishment in the city shall submit an application for a license under this chapter to the chief of police or his designee. Such application shall be made on forms furnished by the city, shall be submitted in the name of the adult entertainment establishment by a natural person authorized to act as an agent of the applicant, and shall include the name(s) of the operator(s) as defined herein and of the owner(s) as defined herein. If the adult entertainment establishment is a corporation, then the agent for purposes of making application for a license hereunder shall be the president or chief executive officer of the corporation. If the adult entertainment establishment is a partnership, the agent for such purposes shall be a general partner. At the time of submitting such application, a nonrefundable application fee payable in cash or by certified check in an amount established by the city's governing body shall be paid to the city to defray, in part, the cost of investigation and report required by this chapter. The chief of police or his designee shall issue a receipt showing that such application fee has been paid. An application shall not be deemed complete until all required information, documentation, and fees have been submitted. It shall be the sole responsibility of the applicant to ensure that the application is complete and accurate. The city shall have no obligation to notify the applicant of deficiencies, and acceptance of an application shall not be construed as a determination of completeness. The application for a license does not itself authorize the operation of, engaging in, conducting or carrying on of any adult entertainment establishment.
(b) Contents. Each application for an adult entertainment establishment license shall include, at a minimum, the following information and documentation, as applicable:
(1) The full true name and any other names used by the applicant, the operator(s) and owner(s);
(2) The present address and telephone number of the applicant, the operator(s) and owner(s);
(3) The previous addresses of the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s), if any, for a period of five (5) years immediately prior to the date of the application and the dates of residence at each;
(4) Acceptable written proof that the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s) are at least eighteen (18) years of age;
(5) The height, weight, color of eyes and hair and date and place of birth of the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s);
(6) Two (2) photographs of the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s) at least two (2) inches by two (2) inches taken within the last six (6) months; (and in addition, the applicant and the operator(s) must agree to be photographed by the city police department prior to issuance of the license applied for);
(7) The business, occupation or employment history of the applicant, the operator(s) and owner(s) for the five (5) years immediately preceding the date of application;
(8) The business license history of the applicant and whether such applicant, in previous operations in this or any other location under license, has had such license or permit for an adult entertainment business or similar type of business revoked or suspended, the reason therefore, and the business activity or occupation subsequent to such action of revocation or suspension;
(9) If the application is made on behalf of a corporation, the name of the corporation, exactly as shown in its articles of incorporation or charter, together with the place and date of incorporation. If the application is on behalf of a limited partnership, a copy of the certificate of limited partnership shall be provided. If one (1) or more of the partners is a corporation, the provisions of this subsection pertaining to corporations shall apply to each such corporation;
(10) The names and addresses of the owner and if applicable, the lessor of the real property upon which the adult entertainment establishment is to be operated, engaged in conducted or carried on and a copy of the lease or rental agreement, if any;
(11) With respect to the applicant, the operator(s) and the owner(s), all convictions, (excluding misdemeanor traffic violations unrelated to driving under the influence of drugs or alcohol) within the past ten (10) years, including a complete description of the crime or violation, the date of the crime or violation, date of conviction including plea of guilty or nolo contendere), jurisdiction and any disposition including any fine or sentence imposed and whether the terms of disposition have been fully completed. Each person required to disclose convictions hereunder shall also provide a signed and notarized consent, on forms prescribed by the GCIC and the NCIC, authorizing the release of his or her criminal records to the city police department;
(12) A complete set of fingerprints of the applicant and the operator(s);
(13) If the person or business entity on whose behalf application for a license is made is doing business under a trade name, a copy of the trade name as properly recorded. If the application is made on behalf of a corporation, a copy of its authority to do business in the state should be provided, including articles of incorporation, and a trade name affidavit, if any, and last annual report, if any;
(14) The address of the premises where the adult entertainment establishment will be operated, engaged in, conducted, or carried on;
(15) A plat prepared by a registered engineer or a registered land surveyor, licensed by the State of Georgia, showing the location of the proposed premises where the adult entertainment establishment will be operated, engaged in, conducted or carried on in relation to the neighborhood, the surrounding zoning, its proximity to any residential area, church, school, public park or children's day care facility, any other adult entertainment establishment, and any establishment licensed by the city to sell alcoholic beverages, beer or wine for consumption on the premises; the survey should depict the location and distance of the property use closest to the proposed premises that would disqualify the property if it were within the prohibited distance pursuant to subsection 9-12-6(a);
(16) Each application for an adult entertainment establishment license shall be verified and acknowledged under oath to be true and correct by:
a. If application is made on behalf of an individual, the individual;
b. If application is made on behalf of a partnership, by a general partner;
c. If application is made on behalf of a corporation, by the president or chief executive officer of the corporation;
d. If application is made on behalf of any other organization or association, by the chief administrative official.
The chief of police or his or her designee may require additional information or documentation reasonably necessary to verify compliance with this chapter and applicable law. Failure to provide such information may be grounds for denial of the application.
(c) Appearance by applicant. The applicant, and any operator(s) or owner(s) identified in the application, may be required to appear before the chief of police or his or her designee for purposes of verification, interview, or submission of additional information. Failure to appear or cooperate shall be grounds for denial of the application.
(d) Investigation; standards for granting of license. The city shall have ninety (90) days from the date of actual receipt of a fully completed application to investigate the facts provided in the application and the background of the applicant, the operator(s) and owner(s). The chief of police or his designee shall stamp the date of receipt of each application on the first page thereof and shall provide the applicant a photocopy of the stamped first page signifying the date of receipt of the application. The chief of police or his designee may search the GCIC and the NCIC to determine whether the applicant, operator(s), and owner(s) appear as part of any record maintained therein. The chief of police shall approve or deny the completed application for an adult entertainment establishment license within ninety (90) days of actual receipt of a fully completed application. If an application is determined to be incomplete, the city may suspend further review of the application until such time as the applicant submits all required information and documentation. The ninety (90) day review period shall not begin until a complete application has been received. The city shall not be required to return an incomplete application or require submission of a new application.
The chief of police shall approve the application if it is determined that all requirements of this section have been satisfied, including but not limited to the following:
(1) The required license application fee has been paid;
(2) The application contains all of the information provided for in subsections (b)(1) through (b)(16) above, and the applicant has made no material misrepresentation of fact in the application;
(3) Neither the applicant nor any of the operator(s) or owner(s) has been convicted or pled guilty or entered a plea of nolo contendere to any crime involving assault, illegal possession or use of a controlled substance, battery, keeping a place of prostitution, pandering, pimping, public indecency, prostitution, sodomy, solicitation of sodomy, masturbation for hire, sexual battery, rape, child molestation, enticing a child for indecent purposes, or any offense included in the definition of a "criminal offense against a victim who is a minor" as defined in O.C.G.A. § 42-1-12 within a period of ten (10) years preceding the date of the application. If there has been any such conviction or plea, then the application shall be denied. For purposes of this chapter, a conviction or plea of guilty or nolo contendere shall be ignored as to any offense for which the applicant was allowed to avail himself of the Georgia First Offender Act unless the applicant is later adjudicated guilty of having violated the terms of his first offender treatment;
(4) Except as may be allowed by virtue of the settlement agreement and/or court order, neither the applicant nor any of the operator(s) or owner(s) has had an adult entertainment establishment license or permit revoked for cause by this city or any other municipal corporation or county located in or out of the State of Georgia within the five (5) year period immediately preceding the date of the application;
(5) The building, structure, equipment and location of the premises of the adult entertainment establishment as proposed by the applicant is in compliance with all applicable laws, including, but not limited to, health, zoning, distance, fire and safety requirements and standards based on information provided by or through other city departments or Clayton County;
(6) The applicant, operator(s) and owners(s) are all at least eighteen (18) years of age;
(7) Except as may be allowed by virtue of the settlement agreement and/or court order, the proposed premises will be located at least the minimum distances set forth in this chapter from any residential use, church, school, public park or children's daycare facility, any other adult entertainment establishment, and any other establishment licensed by the city to sell alcoholic beverages, beer or wine for consumption on the premises pursuant to subsection 9-12-6(a);
(8) The grant of such license will not cause a violation of any law of the State of Georgia or the United States.
The chief of police shall deny the application if the applicant fails to meet any requirement of this section or provides false, misleading, or incomplete information.
(e) Alcoholic beverages. If the applicant, licensee, or owner(s) of an adult entertainment establishment desire to sell or dispense spirituous liquors, beer, wine, or any other alcoholic beverage for on-premises consumption, such applicant shall apply for and obtain all required permits and approvals in accordance with title 9, chapter 2 of this Code, as may be amended, prior to commencing such activity. Approval to sell or dispense alcoholic beverages shall be conditioned upon compliance with all applicable licensing requirements, including the payment of all required fees. The number of adult entertainment establishments permitted to sell or dispense alcoholic beverages for on-premises consumption shall be subject to the limitations set forth in subsection 9-12-7(e) of this chapter.
(Ord. No. 14-25, § 1, 10-27-2014; Ord. No. 26-06, § 4(Exh. D), 5-4-2026; Ord. No. 26-15, § 4(Exh. D), 8-3-2026)

